@baseUrl = http://localhost:9001

# PDF (.pdf) upload cases for POST /api/content-bank/assets/upload.
# All requests require authentication — run "Login" from sessions/sessions.http first.
#
# Limit: 50 MB per .pdf file. Files must start with the `%PDF` magic bytes.
# PDF processing (S3 upload, text extraction, chunk/embed, thumbnail) runs
# asynchronously — the response returns status=pending; poll GET to observe
# the transition to ready / partial / failed and the eventual thumbnail_url.
# Fixture: sample.pdf (tiny 2-page PDF for smoke tests).

### Upload PDF — single file  [protected]
# @name uploadPDF
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample.pdf
--boundary--

> {% client.global.set("pdfAssetId", response.body.results[0].asset_id) %}

### Get PDF asset (poll until status=ready to see file metadata + thumbnail_url)  [protected]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{pdfAssetId}}
Accept: application/json

### Upload PDF + Markdown in a single batch  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample.pdf
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="sample.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ./sample.md
--boundary--

### Upload PDF — bad magic bytes (expects per-file "failed")  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="fake.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

this is plain text pretending to be a PDF
--boundary--

### Upload unknown extension (expects per-file "failed")  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

plain text, not markdown or pdf
--boundary--

### Upload PDF — unauthenticated (expects 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample.pdf
--boundary--

### Delete PDF asset (should clean up S3 objects)  [protected]
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{pdfAssetId}}
